+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse of the veterinarian directory: every specialty it knows, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-SPEC-001]` (requested 2026-08-10). A specialty appears under its stored name, and each holder under it by first name then last name. The page lists specialties, not veterinarians, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. It is a listing rather than a search, and every specialty appears on one page. Nothing in the system links to the page: no navigation entry, and no link from another page. A reader opens it by entering its address, `/specialties.html`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then each one is listed under its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty two veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then both are listed under it by first name and last name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page, with no paging.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a reader who enters the address `/specialties.html`, when the page is requested, then the specialty directory is shown.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it. This reading is provisional — see [Open Questions](#open-questions).
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A specialty's name is shown as stored; it is data rather than translated wording.
+
